Nodes with `data` + `next` pointer. Insert/delete at known node O(1), but access by index O(n) (no random access). Types: singly, doubly (prev + next), circular.

```
// reverse a singly linked list (very common)
Node* prev = nullptr; Node* cur = head;
while (cur) {
    Node* nxt = cur->next;   // save next
    cur->next = prev;        // reverse link
    prev = cur; cur = nxt;   // move forward
}
head = prev;
```

**Floyd's cycle detection**: slow moves 1, fast moves 2; if they meet → cycle. Middle of list: when fast reaches end, slow is at middle.

