**Compile-time (static)**: method **overloading** — same name, different parameters in the same class. **Runtime (dynamic)**: method **overriding** — child redefines parent's method with the same signature; resolved by the actual object type (virtual functions in C++; all non-static, non-final methods in Java).

```
class Animal { void sound(){ print("..."); } }
class Dog extends Animal { @Override void sound(){ print("Bark"); } }
Animal a = new Dog();
a.sound();     // "Bark"  -> runtime polymorphism (object type decides)
```

```
-- 2nd highest salary
SELECT MAX(salary) FROM Employee WHERE salary < (SELECT MAX(salary) FROM Employee);
-- Nth highest (N=3) using LIMIT/OFFSET
SELECT DISTINCT salary FROM Employee ORDER BY salary DESC LIMIT 1 OFFSET 2;
-- employees earning more than their manager (self join)
SELECT e.name FROM Employee e JOIN Employee m ON e.manager_id = m.id WHERE e.salary > m.salary;
-- duplicate names
SELECT name, COUNT(*) FROM Employee GROUP BY name HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;
-- departments with no employees
