cards.body:
- **Mutating state** — Symptom: `items.push(x); setItems(items)` → no re-render · Fix: `setItems([...items, x])`
- **Stale state in updates** — Symptom: `setCount(count+1)` twice → +1 only · Fix: `setCount(c => c + 1)`
- **useEffect infinite loop** — Symptom: effect sets state that is in its own dependency array, or object/array dep recreated every render · Fix: correct deps, useMemo/useCallback, move logic
- **Missing deps** — Symptom: effect uses stale props · Fix: add all used values to deps
- **No cleanup** — Symptom: interval/listener keeps running → memory leak, "set state on unmounted" · Fix: `return () => clearInterval(id)`
- **Missing / index keys** — Symptom: wrong items updated after delete · Fix: stable unique `key={item.id}`
- **Calling instead of passing** — Symptom: `onClick={handle()}` runs on render · Fix: `onClick={handle}` or `onClick={() => handle(id)}`
- **Controlled input without onChange** — Symptom: input can't be typed in · Fix: add onChange or use defaultValue
- **Conditional hooks** — Symptom: hook inside if → "Rendered fewer hooks" · Fix: hooks at top level only
- **Async in useEffect directly** — Symptom: `useEffect(async () => …)` returns a promise · Fix: define async function inside and call it

```
// BUGGY
function Timer() {
  const [s, setS] = useState(0);
  useEffect(() => {
    setInterval(() => setS(s + 1), 1000);   // stale s, no cleanup
  });                                        // no deps -> new interval every render!
  return <p>{s}</p>;
}
// FIXED
useEffect(() => {
  const id = setInterval(() => setS(prev => prev + 1), 1000);
  return () => clearInterval(id);
}, []);
```

